      "message": "The need for this change feels strange to me. That said, I find this structure more readable, but I think the easiest would be:\n```\nauto ref \u003d sk_ref_sp(old);\nthis-\u003eremoveUniqueKey(ref.get());\n```\n\nBut I wonder if this is actually changing behavior. Assuming the `isInCache()` assert above is true, then calling `refResource()` boils down to calling `old-\u003eref()`. That is the same as what `sk_ref_sp()` is doing.  `sk_ref_sp` creates a temporary that should remain alive until its function call returns (at which point the sk_sp is destroyed and that boils down to `old-\u003eunref()`. Did you repro the original bug and confirm this fixed it?",
