      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes I did repo the bug and confirm this fixes it.\n\nThis is the case where the `old` resource has zero refs so we must call it with `this-\u003erefResource()` first since the GrResourceCache must make the first ref on the resource, which also transfers the resource to the non-purgeable queue since when `unref()` is called, it calls `GrResourceCache::notifyARefCntReachedZero` which attempts to remove the resource from the non-purgeable queue. \n\nYour proposed solution doesn\u0027t work since calling `sk_ref_sp()` on `old` hits the assert in GrGpuResource checking that `this-\u003egetRefCnt() \u003e 0`.",
